1
00:00:00,220 --> 00:00:02,000
My wallet does a magic trick.

2
00:00:02,380 --> 00:00:04,600
I put $20 in on Monday.

3
00:00:04,980 --> 00:00:05,320
Ta-da!

4
00:00:05,740 --> 00:00:07,060
By Friday, it's gone.

5
00:00:07,580 --> 00:00:08,200
No smoke.

6
00:00:08,560 --> 00:00:09,200
No rabbit.

7
00:00:09,640 --> 00:00:10,220
Just gone.

8
00:00:10,680 --> 00:00:11,580
The only problem?

9
00:00:11,960 --> 00:00:14,480
I'm the magician, and I have no idea how

10
00:00:14,520 --> 00:00:15,380
the trick works.

11
00:00:15,760 --> 00:00:18,100
And trust me, my wallet has pulled this

12
00:00:18,140 --> 00:00:20,260
trick on me more times than I can count.

13
00:00:20,680 --> 00:00:22,840
So let's figure out how the trick works.

14
00:00:23,260 --> 00:00:25,320
Here are the six biggest mix-ups about

15
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:27,480
budgeting, and once they're gone, this

16
00:00:27,540 --> 00:00:28,600
gets really simple.

17
00:00:28,980 --> 00:00:31,600
Mix-up number one: a budget means no

18
00:00:31,660 --> 00:00:32,160
more fun.

19
00:00:32,520 --> 00:00:34,720
This is why most people never start.

20
00:00:35,080 --> 00:00:37,300
They think a budget is a list of things

21
00:00:37,640 --> 00:00:38,700
you're not allowed to do.

22
00:00:39,120 --> 00:00:40,720
But think about a lunchbox.

23
00:00:41,160 --> 00:00:42,920
You don't only put in vegetables.

24
00:00:43,300 --> 00:00:45,940
You put in a sandwich, some fruit, and

25
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:47,180
maybe a little treat.

26
00:00:47,560 --> 00:00:49,120
A budget works the same way.

27
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:51,040
Say you get $10 a week.

28
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:53,800
You might plan $2 of it for a treat,

29
00:00:54,140 --> 00:00:55,780
like candy or a comic book.

30
00:00:56,160 --> 00:00:58,160
That $2 is part of the plan.

31
00:00:58,520 --> 00:01:00,260
So when you spend it, you're not

32
00:01:00,300 --> 00:01:01,240
breaking the rules.

33
00:01:01,600 --> 00:01:02,540
You're following them.

34
00:01:02,980 --> 00:01:04,000
Fun isn't banned.

35
00:01:04,480 --> 00:01:06,700
Fun just gets its own spot in the box.

36
00:01:07,140 --> 00:01:09,460
Mix-up number two: I don't have enough

37
00:01:09,520 --> 00:01:10,800
money to need a budget.

38
00:01:11,200 --> 00:01:12,940
It's actually the other way around.

39
00:01:13,340 --> 00:01:14,440
Imagine two people.

40
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:16,240
One has $100.

41
00:01:16,580 --> 00:01:17,940
The other has $10.

42
00:01:18,280 --> 00:01:20,340
They both drop $2 on the way home.

43
00:01:20,800 --> 00:01:23,500
For the first person, $2 is just 2 out

44
00:01:23,560 --> 00:01:24,320
of 100.

45
00:01:24,660 --> 00:01:25,720
They barely notice.

46
00:01:26,240 --> 00:01:28,940
For the second person, $2 is 2 out of

47
00:01:29,040 --> 00:01:29,260
10.

48
00:01:29,600 --> 00:01:31,360
That's a fifth of everything they had.

49
00:01:31,760 --> 00:01:33,660
So the less money you have, the more

50
00:01:33,740 --> 00:01:34,740
every dollar matters.

51
00:01:35,340 --> 00:01:37,880
If you have a big bucket of water, a few

52
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:39,660
drops spilling don't hurt much.

53
00:01:40,060 --> 00:01:42,560
If you only have a small cup, every drop

54
00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:43,100
counts.

55
00:01:43,440 --> 00:01:45,540
A budget is how you stop the spills.

56
00:01:45,940 --> 00:01:48,300
Of course, a budget can't fix a pay

57
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:49,460
problem on its own.

58
00:01:49,760 --> 00:01:51,520
But it shows you exactly what you're

59
00:01:51,580 --> 00:01:53,480
working with, so you're not guessing.

60
00:01:53,880 --> 00:01:56,360
Mix-up number three: I can keep it all

61
00:01:56,400 --> 00:01:56,980
in my head.

62
00:01:57,340 --> 00:01:59,300
Your head is great at lots of things.

63
00:01:59,640 --> 00:02:02,020
Remembering every little spend isn't one

64
00:02:02,060 --> 00:02:02,400
of them.

65
00:02:02,760 --> 00:02:05,320
Let's say you buy a $1 snack every day.

66
00:02:05,680 --> 00:02:07,100
One dollar feels like nothing.

67
00:02:07,420 --> 00:02:08,600
But watch what happens.

68
00:02:08,600 --> 00:02:11,120
$1 a day is $7 a week.

69
00:02:11,120 --> 00:02:14,220
$7 a week is about $30 a month.

70
00:02:14,500 --> 00:02:17,680
And in one year, that's $365.

71
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:20,120
One grain of sand is nothing.

72
00:02:20,460 --> 00:02:21,980
Enough grains make a beach.

73
00:02:22,340 --> 00:02:23,260
So write it down.

74
00:02:23,620 --> 00:02:26,100
On paper, in your notes app, anywhere.

75
00:02:26,440 --> 00:02:28,140
What matters is that you can see it.
